  "slug": "learning-deep-16b1",
  "summary": "Three 2026 items apply LLM agents and scalable parsing to repository data and literature, moving curation beyond manual annotation.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is converting heterogeneous public records into explicitly structured, linkable resources through automated curation rather than manual effort alone. The Gemma pipeline anchors samples and experimental designs to ontologies using LLM-supported agentic workflows and is benchmarked against human curation. usiGrabber extracts spectrum identifications from PRIDE mzIdentML files, indexes spectra by USI, and parses over 800M PSMs to prepare proteomics data for machine learning. CoPaLink connects bioinformatics tool mentions in publications to Nextflow workflow code via named-entity recognition and embedding-based entity resolution. What is new is scalable automation applied directly to repository records and literature. The methods differ across domains, so the dominant thread is methodological rather than a shared algorithm.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
